SUMMARY:Grant Flick & Erik McIntyre - Explorations for Violin and Guitar
DESCRIPTION:Buy Tickets!\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				You may have seen and heard Grant Flick’s extraordinary playing and warm stage presence in at least one of his collaborations at KCH with ensembles like Third Coast Swing and Westbound Situation\, or in his duos with Mr. B\, Warren & Flick\, and O’Brien & Flick\, or at his most recent appearance on Melodies & Morsels: France Edition with Zingerman’s Deli. \nWe think you won’t want to miss another innovative collaboration of his coming up on March 19 – this time with guitarist Erik McIntyre! \nIn this special collaboration at Kerrytown Concert House\, Erik and Grant improvise on a mix of standards and deep cuts from their shared stylistic influences (jazz\, country\, blues\, French musette\, etc.). Their music highlights a love of spontaneity while revealing a deep appreciation for intricacy. Through close musical dialogue\, the duo explores a wide range of moods\, embracing the intimacy and transparency unique to a two-person ensemble. Listeners are offered an unfiltered perspective on beauty\, playfulness\, nostalgia\, and contemplation through this improvised acoustic guitar / violin collaboration. \nGrant Flick\, violinErik McIntyre\, acoustic guitar \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Ticket Pricing: Tier 1: $40 (*Student/Youth $30) Tier 2: $35 (*Student/Youth $25) Tier 3: $30 (*Student/Youth $20) \n\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Artists:\n			\n					\n					\n					\n					\n					\n					\n						\n			\n\n				\n														\n													Erik McIntyre\n											\n				\n					acoustic guitar \n			\n			\n				\n			\n\n				\n														\n													Grant Flick\n											\n				\n					violin\, nyckelharpa
URL:https://kerrytownconcerthouse.com/event/erik-mcintyre-grant-flick-explorations-for-violin-and-guitar/
LOCATION:Kerrytown Concert House\, 415 N. 4th Avenue\, Ann Arbor\, MI\, 48104\, United States
CATEGORIES:Kaleidoscope
