SUMMARY:Transfigurations: Han Kang's "The Vegetarian" in Music and Words - Lisa Sung Ensemble
DESCRIPTION:Buy Tickets!\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Korean American jazz pianist Lisa Sung presents an original song cycle inspired by The Vegetarian\, a book by Nobel Prize-winning author Han Kang. Performed by her ensemble in collaboration with the Nam Center for Korean Studies at the University of Michigan\, the concert explores themes from the book: silence\, resistance\, and transformation through sound. Drawing from contemporary jazz and improvisation\, Sung’s compositions translate the novel’s psychological intensity and poetic restraint into an intimate sonic experience. Audiences can expect a performance that blurs literature and music\, inviting deep listening and reflection. \nLisa Sung – Piano\, curatorEva Rosenwald – readerBrynn Hillker – bassMax Welterlen – drumsTae Hoon Yoo (big fire) – readerMarcus Miller – SaxophoneAndrew Bishop – Saxophone & FluteSpecial guest lecturer: Dr. Youngju Ryu\, Professor of Korean Literature & Director of International Institute\, University of Michigan \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Ticket Pricing: Tier 1: $40 (*Student/Youth $30) Tier 2: $35 (*Student/Youth $25) Tier 3: $30 (*Student/Youth $20) \n\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Artists:\n			\n					\n					\n					\n					\n					\n					\n						\n			\n\n				\n														\n													Lisa Sung\n											\n				\n					piano \n			\n			\n				\n	\n	\n\n					\n					 \n				\n					\n					\n					\n					\n					\n					\n						\n			\n\n				\n														\n													Andrew Bishop\n											\n				\n					reeds \n			\n			\n				\n			\n\n				\n														\n													Brynn Hilliker\n											\n				\n					bass \n			\n			\n				\n			\n\n				\n														\n													Dr. Youngju Ryu\n											\n				\n					professor of korean literature \n			\n			\n				\n			\n\n				\n														\n													Eva Rosenwald\n											\n				\n					actor\, musician \n			\n			\n				\n			\n\n				\n														\n													Marcus Elliot Miller\n											\n				\n					reeds \n			\n			\n				\n			\n\n				\n														\n													Max Welterlen\n											\n				\n					drums \n			\n			\n				\n			\n\n				\n														\n													Tae Hoon Yoo (Big Fire)\n											\n				\n					multidiscplinary artist
URL:https://kerrytownconcerthouse.com/event/lisa-sung-ensemble-listening-to-the-vegetarian-music-after-han-kang/
